gc2607-isp (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Colour: desaturate the over-saturated yellow toward ground truth. The
    calibrated CCM/ACM apply a high saturation gain whose blue row subtracts
    most of the blue from a saturated yellow, rendering e.g. a yellow shirt as a
    pure neon far from its true colour. A luminance- and hue-preserving operator
    now scales yellow / orange-yellow chroma toward luminance gray, lifting the
    crushed blue while leaving every other hue and all neutrals untouched.

 -- Vitaly Ostanin <vitaly.ostanin@gmail.com>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 13:30:00 +0300

gc2607-isp (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AWB: gate the gray-world estimator on proximity to the calibrated white
    locus, so a large saturated object (e.g. a brightly coloured shirt) no
    longer biases the white balance and tints neutral whites with a colour cast.
    Falls back to the previous masks when too few near-locus pixels are present.

 -- Vitaly Ostanin <vitaly.ostanin@gmail.com>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 20:10:00 +0300

gc2607-isp (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A/V sync: drive the v4l2loopback output via the streaming API (QBUF) and
    forward libcamera's capture timestamp, so a consumer can sync audio to the
    true capture instant.
  * Denoise (chroma box-blur + temporal luma IIR) now runs on the GPU as compute
    passes, sustaining 30 fps even when high gain enables it.
  * Add --min-fps to set the AE frame-rate floor; the service now defaults to 30.

 -- Vitaly Ostanin <vitaly.ostanin@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 21:00:00 +0300

